# `$findsDeclaredMember(object, "size")`: A GUESS THAT IS ONE OPERATION. If it opened arms like any other guess, six questions in a row would be six tests of one shape with a closed arm each, for an answer that is a boolean either way.
# The walk stamps it with the layouts that are proven or expected of the object, where the records declare a member under the name above each of them, and the emitter asks shape, link and guard.
# `missing`: no record declares it. Unstamped the operation answers false.
# RUN: walk f4 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: FindsDeclaredMember {{*}}key="size" conditions=[{layout=L3 key="size"}] receivers=[L3]
# CHECK: FindsDeclaredMember {{*}}key="count" conditions=[{layout=L3 key="count"}] receivers=[L3]
# CHECK: FindsDeclaredMember {{*}}key="first" conditions=[{layout=L3 key="first"}] receivers=[L3]
# CHECK: FindsDeclaredMember {{*}}key="second" conditions=[{layout=L3 key="second"}] receivers=[L3]
# CHECK: FindsDeclaredMember {{*}}key="third" conditions=[{layout=L3 key="third"}] receivers=[L3]
# CHECK: FindsDeclaredMember {{*}}key="missing"
# CHECK-NOT: receivers=
# RUN(WITHHELD): walk f4 mechanisms=all-Guesses
# WITHHELD: FindsDeclaredMember {{*}}key="size"
# WITHHELD-NOT: receivers=
# PROGRAM-OF: ../../answers/a-declared-member-is-found-while-the-guards-hold.ir
